From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:45:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 086/117] media: iris: print the firmware failure reason on a
 system error

On a fatal error the firmware writes a short text reason (source file,
line, firmware version) into the SFR buffer that the driver allocates and
passes to it, after the size word the driver stores at its start. The
gen2 system error handler only prints the packet type, so the reason is
lost.

Print the text, bounded by the buffer size since the firmware does not
necessarily terminate it, and only when the firmware wrote something.

Idea from Reixo0's commit 19da0a2509bc ("media: iris: print the firmware's
failure reason on a system error") in github Reixo0/linux (no
Signed-off-by); re-implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c        | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
index 7b0ffe28e77a5..dc8aab5c753b6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
@@ -270,6 +270,25 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_session_error(struct iris_inst *inst,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The firmware leaves a text reason for a fatal error (source file, line and
+ * firmware version) in the SFR buffer, after the size word the driver writes
+ * at its start. The text is not necessarily terminated, so bound it.
+ */
+static void iris_hfi_gen2_print_sfr(struct iris_core *core)
+{
+	const char *reason;
+	size_t len;
+
+	if (!core->sfr_vaddr)
+		return;
+
+	reason = (const char *)core->sfr_vaddr + sizeof(u32);
+	len = strnlen(reason, SFR_SIZE - sizeof(u32));
+	if (len)
+		dev_err(core->dev, "firmware failure reason: %.*s\n", (int)len, reason);
+}
+
 static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_system_error(struct iris_core *core,
 					     struct iris_hfi_packet *pkt)
 {
@@ -278,6 +297,8 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_system_error(struct iris_core *core,
 	if (pkt)
 		dev_err(core->dev, "received system error of type %#x\n", pkt->type);
 
+	iris_hfi_gen2_print_sfr(core);
+
 	core->state = IRIS_CORE_ERROR;
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
-- 
